<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mzilikazi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mzilikazi was a nineteenth-century military leader who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> kingdom in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>. His Ndebele moved onto the plateau from the south around 1840, completing the occupation of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> heartland. The Ndebele state drew in part on earlier political precedents, and its arrival marked the end of the Rozvi Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mzilikazi.jpg" alt="Mzilikazi" width="275" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mzilikazi~detail.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
